            <ArticleTitle>Atypical chest discomfort in a 36-year-old man.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/01.JAA.0000484303.43320.cf</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This article focuses on aortic aneurysms and the evaluation of patients with atypical chest pain. A complete and accurate family history is essential. Clinicians should pay close attention to persistence of symptoms and age in patients with atypical chest discomfort who do not have routine confirmatory cardiac findings.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
